Our Python normalizer ports text rules from stats/01-normalize.js; no upstream
code is executed. Color canonicalization is omitted because cells compare only
within the same language. Source prompt text is retained exactly.

API-MRI changes, 2026-10-24:
Retain paper-1 tasks, temperature 1 and valid author-normalized responses.
Split repetitions by rep modulo 3 into reference/calibration/test. Aggregate
reference answers as counts; enroll 132 of 165 author-labelled services.
Hold out 16 whole model labels for unknown calibration and 17 for unknown test.
Derive adaptive candidate rankings and conservative distance/rank-gap gates.
Author-provided model labels and pooled provider provenance are preserved;
this derivative does not independently authenticate original model identities.

Rebuild with relay_audit.identification_build and the two pinned public ZIPs.
The small JSON contains reference counts and prompts, not API credentials or
user prompts. Full response archives are not distributed in this package.

